Phase 3 ① — scoped execution credentials across every runner
============================================================
Date    : 2026-07-27
Cluster : kind-platform-agent (local, $0)
Tenants : acme (4 ns) + globex (1 ns) on one shared cluster — soft tier
Gate    : make check -> 1354 passed, 1 skipped (pre-live)

Claim under test
----------------
Phase 1a proved "the credential is the boundary" on the on-prem path only. This
phase extends it to every runner and to the second dispatch path, and asks the
API server — not our own code — to confirm the boundary.


0. DEFECT FOUND BY LOOKING AT THE LIVE CLUSTER
----------------------------------------------
The RoleBinding that the whole boundary rests on named a ServiceAccount that
did not exist:

    $ kubectl -n acme-dev-observability get rolebinding acme-agent -o jsonpath='{.subjects}'
    [{"kind":"ServiceAccount","name":"platform-agent","namespace":"acme-dev-observability"}]

    $ kubectl -n acme-dev-observability get sa platform-agent
    Error from server (NotFound): serviceaccounts "platform-agent" not found

    $ kubectl -n acme-dev-observability get sa
    NAME      SECRETS   AGE
    default   0         26h

Root cause: `render_rbac` in src/agents/platform/tenancy.py emitted Role +
RoleBinding but never the ServiceAccount the binding points at. Kubernetes
accepts a binding to an absent subject silently, so `kubectl get rolebinding`
showed a healthy grant that no identity could exercise.

It failed CLOSED (nobody got the permission), so nothing broke and nothing
surfaced — the same "no error, just never read" shape as the values-file and
Capsule-deprecation defects. The consequence is not a hole; it is that the RBAC
arm of Phase 1a's proof had never actually been exercised. Phase 1a's DoD read
"Forbidden **or** credential absent", and it was passing on the weaker arm.

Fix: render the ServiceAccount in the same function that renders the binding.
Guard: tests/test_tenancy.py::test_every_binding_subject_is_actually_rendered
asserts each binding subject against what the renderer emits, not against an
expected name.

    $ python scripts/render_tenancy.py acme -e dev | kubectl apply -f -
    serviceaccount/platform-agent created      (x4 namespaces)


1. RAW RBAC — the API server, not our code, is the boundary
-----------------------------------------------------------
A real 1-hour token minted for the acme ServiceAccount:

    $ kubectl auth whoami
    Groups  [system:serviceaccounts system:serviceaccounts:acme-dev-logging system:authenticated]

    A. own namespace (acme-dev-logging)
       can-i patch deployments: yes
       NAME                            READY  UP-TO-DATE  AVAILABLE  AGE
       acme-dev-logging-loki-gateway   1/1    1           1          26h

    B. neighbour tenant (globex-dev-observability)
       can-i patch deployments: no
       Error from server (Forbidden): deployments.apps is forbidden:
       User "system:serviceaccount:acme-dev-logging:platform-agent" cannot list
       resource "deployments" in API group "apps" in the namespace
       "globex-dev-observability"

    C. cluster scope
       can-i list nodes: no
       Error from server (Forbidden): namespaces is forbidden:
       User "system:serviceaccount:acme-dev-logging:platform-agent" cannot list
       resource "namespaces" in API group "" at the cluster scope

This is the first time this arm has actually run — before the fix above there
was no identity to bind.


